cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "OcuTrace: browser-based nystagmus and saccade recording from phone video"
abstract: >-
  Research prototype that turns a phone video of the eyes into a nystagmus and
  saccade recording. Tracks the iris and a fixed facial reference point in the
  browser, and reports fast events, slow phase velocity, beat frequency, square
  wave jerks and tracking quality. Not a medical device and not for diagnosis.
authors:
